  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures Mountain Goats performing at the Music Hall of Williamsburg in Brooklyn, New York, on Saturday, November 8, 2008 [1]. It is the only available recording of this specific show, documented with a clear lineage from the original tape to the digital transfer [1]. The setlist features twenty songs, including several rare tracks such as \"Bring Our Curses Home,\" which has only three archived performances, and \"Mosquito Repellent,\" with six [1]. The concert also includes covers like \"Suedehead\" by Morrissey and \"Supergenesis\" [1]. The performance concludes with a four-song encore, featuring \"Hast Thou Considered The Tetrapod,\" \"Dance Music,\" \"The Mess Inside,\" and \"Palmcoder Yajna\" [1]. The uploader, nyctaper, originally posted the recording on their website, providing both FLAC and MP3 downloads [1]. This show is part of a larger collection of 467 archived performances by the band, with the previous archived show taking place at the Republic on November 3, 2008 [2]. The recording runs for 94 minutes and includes spoken introductions, such as a story about Mario [1].",
